<title>UK: British Energy pulls out of Australia bid.</title>
<headline>British Energy pulls out of Australia bid.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Energy Plc said it had pulled out of a consortium bidding for Australia's Loy Yang A power station.</p>
<p>It had been in a consortium with NRG Energy Inc and CMS Energy Corp of the U.S. to bid for the plant, which is valued at over A$4.0 billion.</p>
<p>Bidding for the plant, which Victoria state is selling, closes on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;While the Loy Yang project held many attractions for us...we will only invest in projects which can enhance shareholder value,&quot; British Energy chief executive Robert Hawley said in a statement.</p>
<p>Two other consortia are reportedly bidding for the plant, one led by AES Corp and one by the American Electric Power Co Inc, both from the U.S.</p>
<p>British Energy said that it would continue to look at investments in the energy sector both in Britain and overseas.</p>
